\paragraph{Network Capacity and Plasticity.}
The primacy bias \citep{nikishin2022primacy} and progressive capacity loss \citep{lyle2022capacity, nikishin2023plasticity} in deep RL networks provide our framework for explaining why the same CIVO trigger produces divergent seed-dependent outcomes (\S\ref{sec:seed_divergence}): early training states may lock in value landscape features that either resist or amplify subsequent CIVO-driven drift.

\paragraph{Diagnostic Methodology.}
Our factorial diagnostic approach follows \citet{henderson2018deep}, who demonstrated the sensitivity of RL results to implementation details, and the large-scale design-choice studies of \citet{engstrom2020implementation} and \citet{andrychowicz2021whatmatters}. We extend this tradition to model-based temporal conditioning, using controlled factor isolation rather than hyperparameter sweeps.

